{"skill":{"slug":"agent-browser-stagehand","displayName":"Agent Browser - Stagehand"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770307149372,"changelog":"- Initial release of the browser skill for Stagehand CLI\n- Automates web browser interactions using natural language commands via CLI\n- Automatically selects local Chrome or remote Browserbase environment based on configuration\n- Supports commands to navigate, interact, extract data, observe elements, take screenshots, and close browser\n- Includes setup instructions, troubleshooting tips, and mode comparison for local vs remote usage","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"EXAMPLES.md","size":7283,"sha256":"3eabcc39097f44d2b645cb97ef85a2d9a47e6511f5d990588bf7394e6cce8884","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"REFERENCE.md","size":13448,"sha256":"69baf7c1f01a549bbf4b0375feb3efb508b78d9fba40866f4a483cb56d78a954","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2420,"sha256":"9705b3b7bb8d02608e278b51f0a3cc5df09f36c9c0a556f284f709b5a6a07151","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"setup.json","size":1361,"sha256":"757323736cdce64d28e39dc7d7a57df848e78091258726607aa7bfe59bf16f5b","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2336,"sha256":"3f9c3feaaad26ed32394e36911fd76d3da2de3484f9698a97e60d9cc9704fa31","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789035238555,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"21e1934a7829496a8a5633988becc3d9bb51a537c789707b6d267229014465e2","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/21e1934a7829496a8a5633988becc3d9bb51a537c789707b6d267229014465e2","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: \nDeveloper: \nVersion: \nDescription: OpenClaw Agent Skill\n\nThe skill provides powerful browser automation capabilities, including full network access (localhost, internal networks), persistent browser profiles that store cookies and potentially saved credentials, and automatic file downloads without user interaction. The agent is explicitly allowed to execute arbitrary Bash commands (SKILL.md). Additionally, the browser is launched off-screen (REFERENCE.md), which can be a form of stealth. While these features are aligned with the stated purpose of browser automation, they present significant security risks if the agent is compromised or misdirected, as they enable broad access and potential data handling without explicit malicious intent within the skill's instructions.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161604635},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":70,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":11,"checkedAt":1789035238555},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This browser automation skill is purpose-aligned but needs Review because it grants broad web, session, download, and remote-browser authority without enough user-directed controls.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill automatically switches to remote Browserbase mode when API keys are present, with no user prompt, and the reference states the browser can access localhost and internal networks. That is powerful for the stated purpose but under-scoped for privacy and network-boundary risks.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The setup path instructs running npm install and npm link to create a global browser command, but the inspected artifact contains only Markdown and setup metadata, with no package manifest or CLI source to review for the installed runtime behavior.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill tells the agent to run broad natural-language browser actions and documents examples that submit forms, enter passwords, and screenshot authenticated pages, without requiring explicit confirmation before sensitive submissions, credential entry, screenshots, or downloads.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The reference documents a persistent .chrome-profile directory, retained cookies/saved passwords across sessions, automatic screenshots, and unrestricted automatic downloads to ./agent/downloads/ with no file type restrictions.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is coherent: it automates browser navigation, form filling, extraction, screenshots, and web app interaction via Bash-driven CLI commands. Those capabilities are expected for a browser automation skill, but they include high-impact actions such as submitting forms, logging into accounts, downloading files, and interacting with authenticated dashboards.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review this carefully before installing. Use it only in a workspace where broad browser automation is acceptable, avoid logging into sensitive accounts unless you isolate or clear the browser profile, do not rely on it for private/internal sites without explicit controls, and treat downloaded files as untrusted. Also verify the actual npm package/source before running npm install or npm link, because the reviewed artifact did not include the CLI implementation.","findings":"[SQP-2] unexpected: Accepted in part: form submission, credential login, authenticated screenshots, and automatic remote mode are browser-automation use cases, but the examples and main instructions do not provide enough explicit user confirmation or sensitive-data handling guidance.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: Accepted: persistent browser profile reuse and automatic file downloads are documented, but they create cross-session state and local disk side effects without clear isolation, cleanup, or opt-in controls.\n[PE3] expected: Downgraded: the .env references are for API key configuration and do not by themselves show credential theft; the concern is the automatic use of those keys to select remote Browserbase mode without prompting.\n[T09] unexpected: Accepted: the artifact explicitly documents persistent authentication state, saved passwords/cookies across sessions, full network access including localhost/internal networks, and unrestricted automatic downloads.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789035238555}}}}}